// Regression: a program may be declarations only, with no rules at all.
// The boot path used to decide "restore the saved program from eeprom" by asking
// whether any INSTRUCTIONS had appeared. A declarations-only program has none, so
// it looked like "nothing to run" and was silently replaced by whatever eeprom.db
// held (csp_eeprom_load re-inits from scratch) -- no error, exit 0, declarations
// just gone. The test now is whether a program was GIVEN, not whether it has rules.
#variable Alpha integer = 11
#variable Beta integer = 22
#variable Gamma integer = 33
